Does an unreachable default provide safe error recovery?

A. No; executing it is undefined behavior
B. Yes; it returns zero
C. Yes; it automatically throws a C++ exception

Answer: A. unreachable states an invariant to the optimizer. It is not a recovery routine or a runtime bounds check.

